# READ_ONLY_RESEARCH（默认模式）

This laptop is the user's only Windows machine (one NVMe disk, Secure Boot on, BitLocker off, WinRE enabled).

Since 2026-10-13 (decision D-17) the project goal is staged whole-machine adaptation on an
external SSD. That does NOT relax this rule: every item below still needs the user's approval
for that exact action. The internal NVMe, Windows, its ESP/BCD and boot entries are never touched.

Never, without the user's separate explicit approval for that exact action:
- Modify Windows EFI, BCD, boot config, NVRAM boot entries, BIOS, Secure Boot, TPM, BitLocker.
- Create/delete/format/resize partitions, write any disk or ESP, run USB writers or macOS installer creation.
- Run `1401.exe` or any admin-requiring 1401 step; install kexts, drivers or system components.
- Send hardware reports, boot logs or device info to third parties (1401 upload dialog defaults to "send").
- Execute unreviewed scripts/binaries (incl. OpCore-Simplify's unpinned iasl download).
- Read/export BitLocker recovery keys, serial numbers, UUIDs or personal data.
- Trigger GitHub Actions, open public issues/PRs, force-push or rebase public branches.

Allowed: git clone, reading source, read-only system queries, detecting tools, and
non-destructive tests in an isolated `%TEMP%` sandbox (source copy, own venv, HOME/TEMP/APPDATA
redirected, proxy pointed at an unreachable address).

A default action of an automated flow is NOT authorization. On a risky step: stop that step,
explain the risk, ask, and continue other safe tasks.
